    {"id": 0, "pos": [-216.716392, -38.774777], "size": [669.527757, 499.326214], "text": "# Tutorial 1 – Basic Shapes\n\n## Drawing shapes\n- Use the left panel to select the shape you want to draw.\n- For polygon shapes, press **SPACE** to finish the shape.\n- To add a note, click the **Note** icon, then click anywhere in the drawing area.\n\n## Selecting shapes\n- Click on a shape to select it.\n- If shapes overlap, clicking the overlapping area will cycle through the overlapping shapes.\n\n## Boolean operations\n- When a shape is selected, press **SPACE** to toggle its boolean operation.\n\n## Shape panel controls\nIn the **Shapes** panel, you can:\n- Reorganize the drawing order (top shapes are drawn first)\n- Select a shape from the list\n- Toggle a shape’s boolean operation directly from the panel\n\n## Selecting polygon or rectangle vertices\n- Select a vertex (small circle) of a polygon or rectangle.\n- Press **SPACE** to toggle between a sharp corner and a rounded corner.\n- When a corner is rounded, use **ARROW UP / ARROW DOWN** to adjust the corner radius.\n\n"}
